From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexei Svitkine <asvitkine@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:56:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [M156] Disable VariationsService HTTP fallback by default

FlyWeb next batch: from branch-heads/8078 2762e65042. Applied after seguridad/siguiente/chromium/0002; applies cleanly (identical diff). No brave-core patches or chromium_src for these files.

Original change's description:
> Disable VariationsService HTTP fallback by default
>
> VariationsService currently retries failed HTTPS seed fetches over HTTP.
> Gate this fallback behind a new kVariationsHttpFallback feature
> (disabled by default) so failed HTTPS variations fetches no longer fall
> back to HTTP unless explicitly enabled.
>
> Note: Since the default state is off, it means only an HTTPS seed could
> re-enable it.
>
> Bug: 588460249, b:554051967
> Change-Id: I0b6c9e7335e0cf2f018e4ca261abf00976f70c85
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8845201
> Reviewed-by: Luc Nguyen <lucnguyen@google.com>
> Commit-Queue: Alexei Svitkine <asvitkine@chromium.org>
> Reviewed-by: Arkadiusz Tomczak <artomczak@google.com>
> Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1750792}

(cherry picked from commit 27d74d49c0e69b037eebcc542e48c835c832910b)

Conflict in variations_service_unittest.cc: on this branch
SeedDateIgnoredOverHttpRetry has no ScopedCommandLine block, so the
ScopedFeatureList line is added as the first statement of the test.

Replaces https://crrev.com/c/8839589, the automatic cherry-pick to this
branch, which carries the same change.

